"environmental_progression\": 0.50,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.10,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.38,\n      \"feedback\": \"The hydrothermal family is literature-supported for proline formation in complex mixtures, but rxn_007 is an extremely aggregated node: the published chemistry used concentrated HCN/HCHO/NH4+ with mineral redox buffers and gave proline as a minor product rather than a clean one-step conversion. rxn_011 remains unsupported for any abiotic L-selective outcome.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_007\",\n        \"rxn_011\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Add NH4+/NH3 and mineral-buffer conditions to rxn_007, or explicitly describe it as a hydrothermal route-family summary node.\",\n        \"Represent the product as a proline-containing mixture or precursor pool unless free proline before workup is specifically supported.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P5\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_001\": 0.65,\n        \"rxn_007\": 0.45,\n        \"rxn_011\": 0.05\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.44,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.44,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.38,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.10,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.35,\n      \"feedback\": \"Coupling discharge chemistry to the hydrothermal node is reasonable at the idea level, but this named path does not explicitly source formaldehyde or justify how discharge products are concentrated and transferred into the hydrothermal setting. rxn_007 still overstates mechanistic knowledge, and rxn_011 is speculative.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_001\",\n        \"rxn_007\",\n        \"rxn_011\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Add a CH2O source module or combine rxn_001 and rxn_002 before the hydrothermal step if the pathway is intended to be complete.\",\n        \"Specify hydrothermal minerals, pressure/temperature, and quenching rather than treating rxn_007 as a direct clean conversion to L-proline.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P6\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_002\": 0.50,\n        \"rxn_007\": 0.45,\n        \"rxn_011\": 0.05\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.43,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.42,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.34,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.10,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.32,\n      \"feedback\": \"This path gives a possible formaldehyde module but no explicit HCN source, and it also leaves the surface-to-hydrothermal transfer unjustified. The hydrothermal node remains a family-level summary rather than a specific reaction, so target achievement is weak even before the unsupported L-enrichment step.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_002\",\n        \"rxn_007\",\n        \"rxn_011\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Add an HCN/NH3 source module or combine this branch with rxn_001 before rxn_007.\",\n        \"Downgrade rxn_007 to a route-family node or add intermediate and mixture nodes rather than direct free-proline formation.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P7\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_008\": 0.40,\n        \"rxn_011\": 0.05\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.40,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.44,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.46,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.08,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.34,\n      \"feedback\": \"Fox-type hot formaldehyde-ammonia chemistry does support proline-releasing hydrolysates, but rxn_008 depicts direct free-proline formation and omits the key distinction between precursor formation and analytical hydrolysis. That is a major fidelity issue relative to the literature, and rxn_011 does not solve L-selectivity.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_008\",\n        \"rxn_011